  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x10C9" flags="0x0">
    <title>SD (abs MAP) - Neutral/Clutch-In | Cyl 1</title>
    <description>SPEED-DENSITY base fuel, cylinder 1, Neutral/Clutch-In. Output = raw fuel quantity (injection time units) vs manifold ABSOLUTE pressure and RPM.

HOW THE ECU USES IT (SD-v3): looked up by FUN_4543E (used when neutral/clutch flag set &gt;=3 cycles and option 0x1826E8 != 3; gate 0x182626 = 0). X input = RAW IAP sensor ADC fef02574 (code patch); axis shown in kPa via X*0.307429-12.6 (provisional 3-bar calibration). Fuel authority: blend curve and tip-in rate gate (0x1824C6) are 0xFFFF, so this map fuels the engine at all throttle openings except sensor-fault limp-home (throttle path).

AXES: X 30 points, 20-300 kPa abs; Y 50 points, 800-16000 RPM.

STARTING VALUES: below 101 kPa = this cylinder's stock IAP map interpolated onto the new axis; above 101 kPa = density-scaled from the stock 0-vacuum column (which stock never actually fuelled from at WOT). Starting point only - tune on a wideband.

REFERENCE: data @0x16BEB8, X axis @0x156244, Y axis @0x16BE54, descriptor @0x156280, code FUN_4543e.

SD-v4.1 VALUES: 535 to 14428 raw (inj. time?).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description>
