  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1133" flags="0x0">
    <title>Boost Spark Retard (MAP x RPM)</title>
    <description>BOOST IGNITION RETARD vs manifold absolute pressure and RPM. SD-v4: used in gear AND in neutral/clutch-in whenever rolling anti-lag is not active. Repurposed stock "Trim B" map (stock values were all 64 = unused).

HOW THE ECU USES IT (SD-v3): FUN_525EE looks it up with X = RAW IAP sensor ADC fef02574 (code patch at 0x52600; stock X was throttle angle) and Y = RPM fef0155C; this table when in gear with clutch out. Output fef01671 -&gt; weighted by fef01674 (enable weight, see "Boost Spark Retard - Enable Weight") -&gt; fef01575 -&gt; FUN_5171C takes the MAX of all retard...

DEFAULT IN SD-v3: 0 retard up to 100 kPa, then ~1 deg per psi of boost (all RPM rows identical) - a conservative starting point, not a tune. Note: the idle/neutral timing path (fef01544, weighted by fef0157A) does not include this retard; it matters only in neutral/clutch-in with the idle path active.

REFERENCE: data @0x188598, X axis @0x18492C, Y axis @0x186F54, descriptor @0x183108, code FUN_525ee.

SD-v4.1 VALUES: 0.00 to 28.83 deg RETARD (64 raw = 0).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration. [Shortened for TunerPro - full text in stock/xdf-master.] [Shortened for TunerPro - full text in stock/xdf-master.]</description>
