  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x118B" flags="0x0">
    <title>TC - Lean Slip Offset | Level 1</title>
    <description>Lean-angle adjustment of the TC slip target for TC level 1 (cornering traction control).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4D9DE looks this curve up by IMU lean angle (RAM 0xFEF0268E, 0 = upright) -&gt; RAM 0xFEF01358, which FUN_4DBD6 subtracts from the target slip (0x8000 = no change) when option 0x18B7C3 != 0x80.

AXES: X axis: 9 points, 0.00 to 60.0 deg (est.).

VALUES (stock SD-v4.1): 32768 to 33178 raw.

TUNING NOTES: Shapes how much the allowed slip changes as the bike leans over. Units match the target-slip curves (X/409.6 % around 0x8000).

CONFIDENCE: Traced in the decompiled code (functions and RAM addresses given above); physical scaling of intermediate values partly inferred.

