  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x11B8" flags="0x0">
    <title>TC - Cut vs Slip Error | Level 8</title>
    <description>Main traction-control torque-cut curve for TC level 8: converts slip error into a torque-reduction demand (proportional term).

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_4DDFC (selected by TC level 0xFEF026D4, or the launch set) looks up slip error (RAM 0xFEF01562 from FUN_4DBD6). The result is scaled by the Lean Gain curve (% at the current lean angle) and added to the slip-rate term, then capped by the per-level maximum (constants 0x18B6EC-0x18B700) -&gt; total cut demand RAM 0xFEF01560. That demand is turned into ignition retard by the "TC - Ignition Retard | Band n" maps and into a throttle limit by the "TC - Throttle Limit" maps.

AXES: X axis: 26 points, 0.00 to 500 raw.

VALUES (stock SD-v4.1): 0.00 to 100 cut demand (raw).

TUNING NOTES: Raising values = harder/faster cut for a given slip error. This curve was previously labelled "ETV - Grip Curve" - its X axis is slip error, not grip opening.

CONFIDENCE: Traced in the decompiled code (functions and RAM addresses given above); physical scaling of intermediate values partly inferred.

REFERENCE: data @0x183FF4, X axis @0x183FC0, descriptor @0x184028, code FUN_4ddfc.</description>
