HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_7C4CE picks the map from pointer table 0x1AD7A4[gear*6 + slot] (gear: N=0..6th=6). The slot comes from per-gear selector bytes 0x18F13A-0x18F155 using the power mode of the active ride mode; stock: PWR 1 -&gt; slot 1, PWR 2 -&gt; slot 2, PWR 3 (and 4) -&gt; slot 3; this map is slot 3. Ride mode presets at 0x18F120 (A), 0x18F127 (B), 0x18F12E (C) set PW = 1/2/3. The result can be further capped by the ETV Limit maps (min()).

AXES: X axis: 23 points, 0.00 to 107 deg (abs. accel angle); Y axis: 39 points, 800 to 16000 RPM.

VALUES (stock SD-v4.1): 0.00 to 74.88 target throttle angle (deg).

TUNING NOTES: Values are target throttle angle in degrees (same scale as the SDS absolute throttle angle; ~118 deg is wide open). Raising cells opens the throttle further for the same grip input - this changes power delivery and is also capped by the limit maps and traction control.

REFERENCE: data @0x199728, X axis @0x19016C, Y axis @0x1996D8, descriptor @0x18F558, code FUN_7c4ce. [Shortened for TunerPro - full text in stock/xdf-master.]</description>
