  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1276" flags="0x0">
    <title>LF - Throttle Limit | Stage B Hold | PWR 2</title>
    <description>Anti-lift (wheelie control) THROTTLE limit map - Stage B Hold | PWR 2.

HOW THE ECU USES IT: FUN_7C62A picks the map from the anti-lift stage counters (RAM 0xFEF00A13 = stage A step 1-4, 0xFEF00A14 = stage B step 1-4; "Entry" = first step, "Hold" = later steps) and, for stage B, the active throttle slot / power mode (0xFEF026D3). X = RPM (0xFEF02AD4), Y = current final ignition timing (0xFEF01567, so throttle closing is coordinated with the ignition retard). FUN_7C944 applies the result as min(limit, normal throttle target) in ETV state 3 (set when the anti-lift flags 0xFEF0096F bit5/6 are on).

AXES: X axis: 14 points, 1000 to 14000 RPM; Y axis: 10 points, 7.00 to 52.0 deg.

VALUES (stock SD-v4.1): 0.87 to 48.61 throttle angle (deg).

TUNING NOTES: Lower cells = anti-lift closes the throttle further. Stage A Hold is all zero in stock form (full close while held). Was "ETV 2 Aux - n".

CONFIDENCE: Traced in the decompiled code (functions and RAM addresses given above); physical scaling of intermediate values partly inferred.

REFERENCE: data @0x1A9054, X axis @0x18FB08, Y axis @0x18FB24, descriptor @0x18FB38, code FUN_7c62a.</description>
