  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x9842" flags="0x0">
    <title>Launch Control :: Engine-Running Confirm Count</title>
    <description>DECODED (v5, confidence MEDIUM): FUN_28BC6: while RPM &gt; 0x18DA8E (500 rpm), after 0x15448B ticks and with START released (FUN_73B52 = 0), counts fef0071C; at this count sets fef00725 bit2 (engine-started flag used by LC). Not a limiter hold timer.

Previous title: Launch Control | Hold suspend timer

FUN_28BC6: if RAM 0xFEF0258E stays above the threshold at 0x18DA8E for this many counts (and condition FUN_73B52 is false) LC is suspended (flag 0xFEF00725 bit2) - most likely the hold-time protection that drops LC if it is held on the limiter too long. Exact signal unconfirmed.

STOCK (SD-v4.1): 25 counts (raw 25 / 0x19).

