  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB001" flags="0x0"><title>MAP IAP - GAIN (slope)</title><description>IAP (manifold) sensor GAIN. FUN_742E2: counts = 7862 + (OFFSET-0x8000) + rawADC*GAIN*32/DIV, clamped 0..65535. DIV is a code immediate at 0x74302: stock 21850 (0x555A), SD-v3 10925 (0x2AAD) so a 3-bar sensor fits the stock internal scale (393.14 counts/kPa, 7862 = 0 kPa).
For a sensor kPa = a x rawADC + b:  GAIN = round(393.14 x a x DIV / 32),  OFFSET = round(32768 + 393.14 x b).
SD-v3 (a = 0.307429, b = -12.6): GAIN 41263 (0xA12F), OFFSET 27814 (0x6CA6). Internal IAP saturates at ~147 kPa - by design; SD fuel and boost spark read the raw ADC instead.
Keep 1023 x GAIN x 32 &lt; 2^31 (GAIN &lt; 65599).

STOCK: 0x81AA (33194). ADDRESS 0x18EF58, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 41263 raw (raw 41263).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="97" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF58" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB002" flags="0x0"><title>MAP IAP - OFFSET (zero)</title><description>IAP (manifold) sensor OFFSET - see IAP GAIN for the formula. SD-v3: 27814 (0x6CA6) for b = -12.6 kPa.

STOCK: 0x8000 (32768). ADDRESS 0x18EF5A, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 27814 raw (raw 27814).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="97" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF5A" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB003" flags="0x0"><title>MAP AP (baro) - GAIN (slope)</title><description>AP (baro) sensor GAIN. FUN_73FD2: counts = OFFSET + ((rawADC x GAIN)/50 &lt;&lt; 5)/437. Stock sensor is kept, so SD-v3 keeps STOCK (SD-v1/v2 had rescaled this, which broke every baro-indexed table).

STOCK: 0x81AA (33194). ADDRESS 0x18EF5E, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 33194 raw (raw 33194).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="97" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF5E" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB004" flags="0x0"><title>MAP AP (baro) - OFFSET (zero)</title><description>AP (baro) sensor OFFSET. SD-v3 = STOCK.

STOCK: 0x1EB7 (7863). ADDRESS 0x18EF60, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 7863 raw (raw 7863).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="97" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x18EF60" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC001" flags="0x0">
    <title>Injector Global Size Scaler (K)</title>
    <description>Global pulsewidth multiplier applied to every primary AND secondary pulse in FUN_4714C: time = deadtime + fuel_time x (K-400)/200. Displayed here as the factor. Stock K=600 = 1.00. FOR LARGER INJECTORS: factor = old_flow / new_flow (e.g. stock to 2x-flow injectors -&gt; 0.50 -&gt; K=500). Fit with matching deadtime tables. This is the cleanest single injector-size knob.

STOCK (SD-v4.1): 1 factor (raw 600 / 0x258).</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="52" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1824C8" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>factor</units>
    <decimalpl>3</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="(X-400)/200">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
