  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC009" flags="0x0">
    <title>Fuel Blend - Tip-In Rate Gate (forces TPS maps)</title>
    <description>Tip-in rate gate (FUN_4916E / FUN_491BC). Compared with fef02604 = throttle opening rate (TP now - TP 4 samples ago, 0x8000 = 0), NOT throttle position. While the rate is at/above this value, and for 0x18267A (4) cycles after it drops below, the ECU forces 100% TPS-map fuel (blend weight fef011CA = 256). Stock 33282 = TP rise of 1.41 deg within 4 samples. 0xFFFF disables it (SD-v2 and later race bins do this so the speed-density map keeps authority on tip-in). Earlier XDFs showed this as a 91.4 deg WOT gate - that was wrong.

STOCK (SD-v4.1): 90.00 deg/4 samples (raw 65535 / 0xFFFF). ADDRESS 0x1824C6, 16-bit.

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="53" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="2" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1824C6" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>deg/4 samples</units>
    <decimalpl>2</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="(X-32768)/364.08">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC00A" flags="0x0"><title>Neutral/Clutch Fuel-Map Gate</title><description>Pressure gate used by FUN_4543E (neutral/clutch fuel map allowed only if input &gt;= gate) and FUN_455E6 (neutral dwell counter, input = vacuum fef02628). SD-v3: FUN_4543E input is the raw IAP ADC (0-1023), so this must stay 0 or the neutral map is never used. Side effect vs stock: the neutral/clutch-in map also stays active under boost (stock dropped it at IAP &gt;= baro); those maps are boost-capable.

STOCK: 7863 (0x1EB7). ADDRESS 0x182626, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 0.00 raw (raw 0).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="95" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x182626" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC00C" flags="0x0"><title>IAP Sensor Circuit-Low Threshold (raw ADC)</title><description>Raw IAP ADC below which the circuit-low DTC starts debouncing (FUN_39076). Unchanged.

STOCK: 20. ADDRESS 0x1547E0, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 20 raw (raw 20).</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="95" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1547E0" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xC00B" flags="0x0"><title>IAP Sensor Circuit-High Threshold (raw ADC)</title><description>Raw IAP ADC (fef02574) above which the circuit-high DTC starts debouncing (FUN_390F8/FUN_3917A, debounce 0x1547E6 = 750). Stock 983 (~4.8 V) = ~290 kPa on the 3-bar sensor, which would fault under high boost. SD-v3: 1022 (only a shorted/saturated sensor trips).

STOCK: 983. ADDRESS 0x1547E2, 16-bit.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 1022 raw (raw 1022).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="95" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x1547E2" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x20001" flags="0x0">
    <title>Decel Fuel Cut :: Resume RPM (Gear x Cylinder)</title>
    <description>Decel fuel-cut RPM band per gear and cylinder (warm engine). FUN_49E10 picks one row each cycle: clutch pulled (FUN_7626A) -&gt; "Clutch-in"; neutral or FUN_365B8 -&gt; "Neutral / other"; otherwise the row for the engaged gear. Each cell is a pair: RESUME RPM (lower edge, fef01270) and CUT RPM (upper edge, fef01268). FUN_4A256 runs the cut state machine with that band (closed throttle / decel conditions decided elsewhere). Cold engine (ECT &lt;= 0x1826A3) uses the separate "Decel Fuel Cut :: Cold | ..." constants instead. Stock clutch-in row = 25200/25300 rpm = no decel cut with the clutch pulled. Raise both values to stop decel fuel-cut in that gear (e.g. for a smoother corner entry or to keep fuel in the exhaust); keep CUT &gt; RESUME.

This table: RESUME (lower) RPM. Data 0x18251C, 8 rows x 4 cyl, 32-bit stride (interleaved with the CUT table).</description>
