CAUTION: this monitor protects the throttle-by-wire / engine-position / ECM integrity / oil-pressure system. Turning it off hides a real fault and can stop the ECU from entering its fail-safe (for wheel-speed codes: traction/launch control keep running on bad data). Not recommended.

DTCs controlled by this byte: P2158 #4 - Vehicle speed sensor B (rear wheel speed from ABS unit).
STOCK (SD-v4.1): 0x80 (monitor ON). Several stock calibrations ship with many emissions monitors switched off.
ADDRESS 0x154986. Monitor code checks "byte == 0x80" (example: FUN_32A24 for P2123). Use a full byte value of 0x80 or 0x00 - other values also count as OFF.
Related: the lamp toggles in "Diagnostics - DTC Lamp Control" only hide the lamp; this switch stops the monitor itself.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="54" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x154986" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x80</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
