  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD100" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Enable</title><description>128 (0x80) = rolling anti-lag enabled; anything else = disabled (START button behaves stock: launch control long-press works again). Default 128.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 0.00 raw (raw 0).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF000" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>raw</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD101" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Min Coolant Temp</title><description>ALS will not arm below this coolant temperature (RAM 0xFEF026BD). Default 60 C.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 60 deg C (raw 96).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF001" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg C</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X*0.9375-30"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD102" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Min Rolling Speed</title><description>ALS arms only while the FRONT wheel speed (RAM 0xFEF0263A) is at or above this. Below it, holding START keeps its stock launch-control function. Default 20 km/h.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 20 km/h (raw 2560).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF002" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>km/h</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/128"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD103" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Capture Grip Angle (WOT)</title><description>With START held and rolling, the moment grip angle (RAM 0xFEF025EC, abs. accel angle; ~107 deg = full) reaches this, the current RPM is captured and held. Default 90 deg.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 90.00 deg grip (raw 32767).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF004" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg grip</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/364.08"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD104" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Release Grip Angle</title><description>If the grip drops below this while active, ALS releases (re-opening past the capture angle re-captures). Default 60 deg. Keep below the capture angle.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 60.00 deg grip (raw 21845).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF006" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>deg grip</units><decimalpl>1</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/364.08"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD105" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Min Capture RPM</title><description>ALS will not engage if RPM at capture is below this (avoids bogging at low RPM). Default 3000. Must be greater than the hysteresis.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 3000 RPM (raw 7680).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF008" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD106" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Max Capture RPM</title><description>Captured RPM is clamped to this. Keep below the in-gear fuel-cut limiter (11,200 stock) and the ignition-cut limiter (12,000). Default 10500.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 10500 RPM (raw 26880).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF00A" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD107" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Hold Hysteresis</title><description>Spark returns when RPM falls this far below the captured RPM (cut is ON at &gt;= captured RPM). Smaller = tighter hold, harsher cut. Default 150 rpm.

SD-v4.1 VALUE: 150 RPM (raw 384).

DIFFERS FROM STOCK 5JCZSJ40 in the SD-v4.1 bin (changed by the race software): free-text "stock" remarks above describe the stock calibration.</description><CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="96" /><EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0xBF00C" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" /><units>RPM</units><decimalpl>0</decimalpl><datatype>0</datatype><unittype>0</unittype><DALINK index="0" /><MATH equation="X/2.56"><VAR id="X" /></MATH></XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xD108" flags="0x0"><title>ALS Max Active Time</title><description>Safety timer: after this long continuously active, ALS drops out and stays off until START is released. Counted in the ~5 ms task (period inferred, verify on the bench). Default 2000 counts = 10 s.

